  "about": "Hong Kong dollar settlement closures (Hong Kong banks; HKMA's CHATS), 2008-2027: the weekday general holidays of the General Holidays Ordinance (Cap. 149) as the Government gazettes them each year, the substitute days already applied (a holiday on a Sunday is the next day; the day following Mid-Autumn, National Day or Christmas when the day itself is a Sunday or another holiday). Banks close on general holidays, not only the statutory ones. Lunar dates make rules unusable past the published year, so each holiday is a table of its gazetted dates. Saturdays are general holidays but not settlement days, so they are left out. One-off: 3 September 2015 (Special Holiday (3 September 2015) Ordinance). Checked against GovHK's 2023 list (as published 2022-05-13) and the State's yearly lists on gov.hk; the vacanza holidays library agrees on every year except 3 October in 2012, 2017 and 2023, which it adds and the gazetted lists don't have. Coverage ends at the latest published year (2027).",
